202610182341","idp_filedate":1792366914000,"nhcTitle":"Off the East Coast of the United States","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area is developing along a  frontal boundary tonight off the southeast coast of the United  States. This low is likely to move slowly and erratically over the  next couple of days while it initially remains non-tropical. Later  this week, if the system stays over the Gulf Stream, environmental  conditions could become more conducive for the low to develop some  subtropical characteristics. A subtropical cyclone could form over  the second half of this week as the system begins moving generally  northeastward, offshore of the eastern United States. Regardless of  development, this system will cause high winds, coastal flooding,  and dangerous surf along portions of the U.S. East Coast. Please  consult statements and warnings from local National Weather Service  offices and the Weather Prediction Center for more information,  along with High Seas Forecasts and Storm Warnings issued by the  National Weather Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.02055651271871,6.294640532589432],[-92.81509884934961,6.3030647797065615],[-92.61060623479115,6.312651003710343],[-92.40732529286493,6.323444948706238],[-92.20550264739248,6.335492358799708],[-92.00538492219538,6.348838978096215],[-91.8072187410952,6.363530550701221],[-91.61125072791351,6.379612820720188],[-91.4177275064719,6.397131532258577],[-91.22689570059194,6.416132429421849],[-91.03900193409518,6.436661256315467],[-90.85429283080322,6.458763757044893],[-90.6730150145376,6.482485675715587],[-90.4954151091199,6.507872756433011],[-90.32173973837172,6.53497074330263],[-90.1522355261146,6.563825380429901],[-89.98714909617011,6.594482411920289],[-89.82672707235983,6.626987581879255],[-89.67121607850534,6.661